Subject: [PATCH] esp32s3: retain the completed boundary for queued capture

When the video completion callback supplies another owned buffer, VSYNC is
already at a complete frame boundary. Arm that buffer immediately rather
than waiting for and discarding the next whole sensor frame. DMA remains
quiescent throughout the callback and is never restarted if it stopped
capture (including FIFO exhaustion). Initial capture still waits for its
first boundary, preserving complete-frame alignment.

diff --git a/arch/xtensa/src/esp32s3/esp32s3_cam.c b/arch/xtensa/src/esp32s3/esp32s3_cam.c
--- a/arch/xtensa/src/esp32s3/esp32s3_cam.c
+++ b/arch/xtensa/src/esp32s3/esp32s3_cam.c
@@ -367,11 +367,13 @@ static int IRAM_ATTR cam_interrupt(int irq, void *context, void *arg)
                 }
               else
                 {
-                  /* Restart capture for next frame */
+                  /* The callback supplied the next owned buffer. This
+                   * VSYNC is already its start boundary; do not discard
+                   * another complete sensor frame before arming DMA.
+                   */
 
-                  priv->vsync_cnt = 0;
-
-                  cam_prepare_frame(priv, false);
+                  priv->vsync_cnt = 1;
+                  cam_prepare_frame(priv, true);
                 }
             }
         }
